                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer – this game was received as part of a challenge among friends.\n\nTo say that this title is \"heavily inspired by\" Lunar Lander is putting it mildly.  This is a buggy clone with additional \"features\" that don't add to the experience.\n\nThe physics are just far enough off to feel wrong.  Thrust mostly seems to work, but acceleration trails off far faster than it should.  The maps themselves did seem random to a degree, but every one was “fly to the right for half the map and then start looking for a landing zone”.  The landing areas themselves were usually visible, but buggy.  I had multiple instances where I “landed” on the right patch of ground, only to keep falling through the terrain and blow up.  I also had at least one level where I fell through a landing zone and still managed to beat the stage by drifting into a second landing zone inside the terrain I had just fallen through.\n\nYou can select from multiple ships at the beginning, but the only noticeable change was in the amount of fuel each ship started with.  The random events after beating a level all gave the same options of more points, more fuel, or an extra life.  Even the scoring function bugged out in at least one run.  Score seems to be calculated as remaining fuel (more or less), but I had one instance where I only completed the first stage and suddenly had over 19000 points.  The average score would probably be more like 200.\n\nOn the plus side, the game ran without issues, and is small enough that you only have to regret a tiny amount of wasted disk space.",
